.TH VIBEOS-INSTALLER 1 "2026-11-17" "vibeos 0.1.1" "VibeOS"
.SH NAME
vibeos-installer \- App Installer: installs and uninstalls software packages on VibeOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vibeos-installer
.RI [ FILE.deb ...]
.br
.B vibeos-installer \-\-install
.I NAME
.br
.B vibeos-installer \-\-uninstall
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
App Installer shows a package before anything changes: its app's name and icon, the version, the sizes, its
description, and what installing it will do. A new install is asked once; when a version is installed already it
shows both versions and which is newer, and asks to replace it (Replace with the file's version), says so plainly when
the file's version is OLDER, and offers Reinstall for the same version. The check before that (PackageKit's simulation)
names the other packages it installs too, or says which dependency cannot be met. A package installs with full rights
on the device, and the page says so.
.PP
Installing and uninstalling go through PackageKit; polkit asks for the password, App Installer never sees it.
Back while a package installs takes the window home and the install goes on; a notification says how it ended.
.PP
Opened from the app drawer it starts at a page that says what it does, with Choose a package. It is the default app
for .deb files in the VibeOS session (Files opens them with it).
.PP
.B \-\-install
.I NAME
installs the package NAME from the software sources (apt's), with the same page and questions;
.B \-\-uninstall
.I NAME
asks to uninstall it, with the space freed and the other packages that would go with it. It will not uninstall
VibeOS's own packages, the shell (gnome-shell, mutter), the session, or packages that are Essential or of priority
required.
.PP
Other apps (Software) use its D-Bus interface,
.B vibeos.Installer1
on
.I /vibeos/Installer
(bus name vibeos.Installer): InstallPackage, InstallFile, RemovePackage, Cancel and GetState, with the signals Progress
and Finished. A call from another app never opens App Installer's window: polkit asks for the password, and a sheet
over the calling app asks a question when there is one (a replacement, a downgrade, other packages, an uninstall).
The interface is documented in
.IR /usr/share/dbus-1/interfaces/vibeos.Installer1.xml .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/gnome-mimeapps.list
Makes App Installer the session's default for application/vnd.debian.binary-package and application/x-deb. A default
the user chooses (in
.IR ~/.config/mimeapps.list )
comes first.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/vibeos-installer/
A copy of a .deb opened from somewhere PackageKit cannot read (a network folder, a document portal), and when the
software sources' lists were last refreshed (they are refreshed when older than six hours).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VIBEOS_INSTALLER_DEMO
Plays canned states instead of asking PackageKit: nothing is installed or removed. A comma-separated list of
settings, such as
.B installed=1.2-1,deps=2,auto
(the list is in the source, apps/installer/src/inst-demo.h).
